INSERT OR REPLACE INTO "DataQuest" ("ID","Name","StartType","StartName","StartRegionID","AcceptText","Description","SourceName","SourceText","StepType","StepText","StepItemTemplates","AdvanceText","TargetName","TargetText","CollectItemTemplate","MaxCount","MinLevel","MaxLevel","RewardMoney","RewardXP","RewardCLXP","RewardRP","RewardBP","OptionalRewardItemTemplates","FinalRewardItemTemplates","FinishText","QuestDependency","AllowedClasses","ClassType","LastTimeRowUpdated") VALUES (20192,'The Lost Stone',0,'Captain Herly',51,'assignment','Welcome back. I have been watching your training and you seem to be blessed with many skills. Those skills will come in handy in the near future. I have been sending reports of your progress to my superiors at the Defenders hall in Camelot and they have decided that it is time to [test your limits and skills].','','Seek out Gavon Montgomery at Caifelle. (whisper: <your name>)|||','6|0|0|3','Seek out Gavon Montgomery at Caifelle. (whisper: <your name>)|Get the missing stone from the urchin rabblerousers south of Caifelle. (1/2)|Get the missing stone from the urchin rabblerousers south of Caifelle. (2/2)|Return the plain flat gray stone to Gavon Montgomery.','|||cq_small_flat_gray_stone','<your name>|||','Gavon Montgomery;51|urchin rabblerouser;51|urchin rabblerouser;51|Gavon Montgomery;51','Greetings Friar. I see that your trainer received the message fromt he Defenders. What is your name? We have quite a task ahead of us. I was once a Scout for the Defenders of Albion before I hurt my leg. Since I can no longer do my duty, the Defenders have helped set me up s as merchant. It''s not what I had planned to be doing , but it puts food on my table. Even though I am not an active member of the Defenders, I still do what I can to help. Lately that has meant [tracking down lost objects]. As you may know, the Defenders of Albion are always searching for better ways to defend the realm from enemies. Our duty is hard, for these days we face not onlythe enemies that nip at our borders but also the ones that exist amongst us. Anything that can be done or used to make our fight a little easier is always well supported among the Defenders. That is [why I was sent] here. One of the Inconnu that has been helping us to defend the realm against the Drakoran located and recovered a stone that seems to weaken the Drakoran. Our Theurgists back in Camelot wish to examine and study this stone so that it can possibly be duplicated and used to aid us in this fight. If we [only had it now]! This Inconnu was coming back from getting the stone when he was attacked and overpowered by a pack of urchin rabblerousers. They stole the stone and ran off into the wilds when the Inconnu mandaged to crawl back here. So far no one has been able to capture the little rabblerouser that has it. Go now and seek out the urchin rabblerouser that has it. They are tricky and throw it around, so keep trying until you find it. We are counting on you. Were you able to find the stone? The Defenders in Albion are waiting for it so they can begin trying to duplicate it. I must send it to them soon. This isn''t the stone I seek! I was told it was plain, flat, gray stone. It may have special properties, but the Defenders will have to investigate it. Did you find another stone? This stone doesn''t look like it will do much, but we hope that it will. I shall get this over to Camelot right away. The Defenders of Albion sent this over for the person who was able to recover the lost stone. Here take it, and know that you have helped to defend the realm!|||Greetings Friar. I see that your trainer received the message fromt he Defenders. What is your name? We have quite a task ahead of us. I was once a Scout for the Defenders of Albion before I hurt my leg. Since I can no longer do my duty, the Defenders have helped set me up s as merchant. It''s not what I had planned to be doing , but it puts food on my table. Even though I am not an active member of the Defenders, I still do what I can to help. Lately that has meant [tracking down lost objects]. As you may know, the Defenders of Albion are always searching for better ways to defend the realm from enemies. Our duty is hard, for these days we face not onlythe enemies that nip at our borders but also the ones that exist amongst us. Anything that can be done or used to make our fight a little easier is always well supported among the Defenders. That is [why I was sent] here. One of the Inconnu that has been helping us to defend the realm against the Drakoran located and recovered a stone that seems to weaken the Drakoran. Our Theurgists back in Camelot wish to examine and study this stone so that it can possibly be duplicated and used to aid us in this fight. If we [only had it now]! This Inconnu was coming back from getting the stone when he was attacked and overpowered by a pack of urchin rabblerousers. They stole the stone and ran off into the wilds when the Inconnu mandaged to crawl back here. So far no one has been able to capture the little rabblerouser that has it. Go now and seek out the urchin rabblerouser that has it. They are tricky and throw it around, so keep trying until you find it. We are counting on you. Were you able to find the stone? The Defenders in Albion are waiting for it so they can begin trying to duplicate it. I must send it to them soon. This isn''t the stone I seek! I was told it was plain, flat, gray stone. It may have special properties, but the Defenders will have to investigate it. Did you find another stone? This stone doesn''t look like it will do much, but we hope that it will. I shall get this over to Camelot right away. The Defenders of Albion sent this over for the person who was able to recover the lost stone. Here take it, and know that you have helped to defend the realm!','|||cq_small_flat_gray_stone',1,7,50,'0|0|0|700','0|0|0|3300',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cq_alb_defender_s_sleeves','','','2','DOL.GS.Quests.ClassicQuestStep','2026-10-08 06:15:00');
