ould be for you to take the initiative and go after him first. He is Southwest of here, under a tree outside the main camp. Nice work, I''m glad Rip won''t be bothering us anymore. I wish I had courage like yours. Then my little brother wouldn''t be in danger. Will you please [help] me take care of Priest Thaxtix? Please go and kill Priest Thaxtix for me. You might need to bring a few friends along to help because Thaxtix is usally surrounded by his lesser priests. Bring back proof that he''s dead, so I can turn it in and then quit the Svatalfar. Here is some silver for you also, to reimburse some of what you''ve spent on travel. Taking a horse from Huginfell to Myrkwood and back can get expensive. You''re back! Did you bring proof that you killed Priest Thaxtix? I don''t know how to thank you, you''ve done so much for me and my brother. Perhaps you can get some use out of these boots. I came by them honestly, and they have some useful properties. Thanks gain for your help.||What are you doing here, spying? Give me one good reason I shouldn''t just kill you right now. So! You know my real name, do you? Keep your voice down, there are unfriendly ears nearby. My brother Thrand must have told you. I don''t blame him for worrying, I''m in real trouble this time. I got involved with these treacherous Svartalfar and now they want me to [kill someone]. Shhhh! Not so loud. Yes, murder. You''re probably not familiar with the Svartalfar, so before I ask you to help me I''ll explain a little about them. The Svartalfar, the Arachites and the Varulv are all involved in a long-standing dispute over the Myrkwood area. The Svartalfar think that they were there first and that the other two groups are invading their [territory]. The three factions are constantly fighting amongst themselves, sometimes in open combat, but more often they send agents to murder key personalities and sabotage plans. The Svartalfar have become adept at sneak attacks and assassinations and are pretty unscru