INSERT OR REPLACE INTO "DataQuest" ("ID","Name","StartType","StartName","StartRegionID","AcceptText","Description","SourceName","SourceText","StepType","StepText","StepItemTemplates","AdvanceText","TargetName","TargetText","CollectItemTemplate","MaxCount","MinLevel","MaxLevel","RewardMoney","RewardXP","RewardCLXP","RewardRP","RewardBP","OptionalRewardItemTemplates","FinalRewardItemTemplates","FinishText","QuestDependency","AllowedClasses","ClassType","LastTimeRowUpdated") VALUES (20650,'Black Plague',0,'Sister Elaydith',10,'continues','About sever days ago, one of the city guards became suddenly ill during the night and I was called to her bedside. The guard was crying and in severe pain. She said that her back felt like it was on fire. I rolled her on her side to look at her back and the smell of [rotthing flesh] filled the air.','','Good. I will need all the help I can get. I would like you to go meet with Berenger Brenner. He is the guardian of one of the latest people to show signs of the disease. I would like you to try and discover anything you can about the strange illness. I will try to make another potion to cure it while you are gone. May the light of Camelot shine upon you, ______.|||||||','4|4|2|2|0|10|0|3','Meet with Berenger Brennan, who watches over Gaevin.|Speak with Gaevin Sebryn.|Take the sealed letter to Gaevin''s brother Keener Woedin in Ludlow.|Bring Keener''s note back to Gaevin.|Go to Dartmoor and kill a Dartmoor pony for the horse fungus.|Return to Sister Elaydith.|Go into Darkness Falls and kill Malroch the Cook.|Return to Sister Elaydith.','||cq_sealed_letter_for_keener|cq_note_for_gaevin|cq_horse_fungus;40|||cq_malroch_s_ladle','|||||||','Berenger Brennar;10|Gaevin Sebryn;10|Keenar Woedin;1|Gaevin Sebryn;10|Dartmoor pony;1|Sister Elaydith;10|Malroch the Cook;249|Sister Elaydith;10','|What are ye looking at? Didn''t your sire ever teach you not to stare? Anyway, it''s not important. I told the clerics everything I know about how I became sick. I went to bed one night feeling fine and I awoke the next morning with my back feeling like I had slept on a bed of hot coals. I haven''t left the city in the past few weeks and I haven''t been around sick people, at least none that looked [sick]. I have heard rumors spreading around the city about people falling ill, but the guards are keeping a tight lip if you ask them what is happening. I think the king is trying to keep this sickness a secret so people don''t panic. Can I tell you my own [secret]? I am really scared, ______. I am putting a brave face on so that the city guard, Berenger, doesn''t lock me up. I don''t think I will live to see the next full moon. Can you do me a [favor], ______?'' I need a message delivered to my hometown so they know what is going on. If I die, I don''t want them to think I left home because of them. I just needed to get out and see the world, [understand]? I am sure you do. You seem the adventurous sort yourself. Now take this sealed letter to my brother, Keener, in Ludlow. He will make sure my parents get it. Tell him not to worry about me. He will know something is wrong when he gets my letter because I haven''t tried to wrote to my parents in years. [Hopefully], the cleric will find a cure before you return. If not, I may not be hear to learn of any news you bring back. Now get out of here! I am tired of looking at your ugly mug. Thank you for bringing me this note. I am glad my parents know I am sick, but I am not sure I remember your name, <Class>. I haven''t been [feeling] well lately at all. I can''t lie down to sleep anymore. It causes so much pain if I touch the sores. I am getting sicker and I am so scared. A [strange man] came to visit me while you were gone. He was dressed in long robes and said he was Marquis Sabonach. That man did not look like a noble at all. He whispered some strange words in my ear and said I would be [ok]. He lied. I even feel worse than yesterday. My body hurts too much for me to try lying down again. I don''t know what I am going to do. I hope the Healer has a cure for me soon. Could you ask Berenger if he has heard anything yet? I know Berenger thiks I have lost my mind but I am fooling him. Tehe haha.||What are ye looking at? Didn''t your sire ever teach you not to stare? Anyway, it''s not important. I told the clerics everything I know about how I became sick. I went to bed one night feeling fine and I awoke the next morning with my back feeling like I had slept on a bed of hot coals. I haven''t left the city in the past few weeks and I haven''t been around sick people, at least none that looked [sick]. I have heard rumors spreading around the city about people falling ill, but the guards are keeping a tight lip if you ask them what is happening. I think the king is trying to keep this sickness a secret so people don''t panic. Can I tell you my own [secret]? I am really scared, ______. I am putting a brave face on so that the city guard, Berenger, doesn''t lock me up. I don''t think I will live to see the next full moon. Can you do me a [favor], ______?'' I need a message delivered to my hometown so they know what is going on. If I die, I don''t want them to think I left home because of them. I just needed to get out and see the world, [understand]? I am sure you do. You seem the adventurous sort yourself. Now take this sealed letter to my brother, Keener, in Ludlow. He will make sure my parents get it. Tell him not to worry about me. He will know something is wrong when he gets my letter because I haven''t tried to wrote to my parents in years. [Hopefully], the cleric will find a cure before you return. If not, I may not be hear to learn of any news you bring back. Now get out of here! I am tired of looking at your ugly mug. Thank you for bringing me this note. I am glad my parents know I am sick, but I am not sure I remember your name, <Class>. I haven''t been [feeling] well lately at all. I can''t lie down to sleep anymore. It causes so much pain if I touch the sores. I am getting sicker and I am so scared. A [strange man] came to visit me while you were gone. He was dressed in long robes and said he was Marquis Sabonach. That man did not look like a noble at all. He whispered some strange words in my ear and said I would be [ok]. He lied. I even feel worse than yesterday. My body hurts too much for me to try lying down again. I don''t know what I am going to do. I hope the Healer has a cure for me soon. Could you ask Berenger if he has heard anything yet? I know Berenger thiks I have lost my mind but I am fooling him. Tehe haha.||Praise the Church, you have returned! There have been more people coming down with the plague. Luckly, I have found a way to figure out who is [sick] and who isn''t. This potion gives me the ability to see who is sick. I was just about to drink some more before you came in.||','||cq_sealed_letter_for_keener|cq_note_for_gaevin||cq_horse_fungus||cq_malroch_s_ladle',1,37,50,'0|0|0|0|0|0|0|0','0|6918022|13836044|6918022|0|13836044|0|13836044',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cq_alb_unstoppered_wondrous_potion_alb','This one potion should be more than enough. You can keep the other potion for yourself. It''s a very powerful potion, so use it when in dire straights. I must begin to cure the other stricken people. You have earned a friend for life, ______. I shall remember your name if I am ever in need of help again.','','','DOL.GS.Quests.ClassicQuestStep','2026-10-08 06:15:00');
